# Relay shipped read catalog ledger: binds each released Template name to its body and risk class.
#
# Each line is: NAME RISK_CLASS DIGEST STATUS
#   NAME        ^[a-z][a-z0-9_.]*$, the Template name in catalog.toml
#   RISK_CLASS  read or mutate
#   DIGEST      64 lowercase hex, SHA-256 of the Template's canonical body (its body text
#               and ordered slot declarations) computed by the daemon's own Template parser
#   STATUS      active or withdrawn
#
# Grammar: a line starting with # in column 0 is a comment; empty lines are ignored; every
# other line has exactly four fields separated by single spaces, with no leading or trailing
# whitespace. No inline comments (a trailing "# note" is malformed). LF line endings only.
# Each NAME appears at most once.
#
# Policy (ADR-0021, amendment 2026-10-15):
#   - Append only. A released entry never changes, except active to withdrawn.
#   - Withdrawn entries stay forever and their names are never reused.
#   - A changed body or class ships under a new name.
#   - Appends land on main first: entries are compared by position against every release tag.
#
# To get the line for a new Template, run `cargo test catalog_names_match_ledger` in daemon/;
# its failure output prints it. Checked by that test and by scripts/catalog-ledger.sh.
proc.list read 367904651b393c95fb1459eb4ec3a3a5ddcf8eec4bbb9cf7405f767cdc9488e4 active
service.status read 0d7eb70b4fac2abbd1589fb531a032fba76c2bd55954875410712383449db7e2 active
disk.usage read 0caa55b3fe9e93e360b2caa020ee5a35ebcab39699365fc436448243f8ec9845 active
net.listening read 9643c99d9ee2eb324ea079769dc51966dada1bd3a0a9fc135a25197fc8c1c0f4 active
